### ====================================================================
### REST Client Test File for VS Code (REST Client Extension)
### Final Exam - Blog Platform Endpoints Verification
### ====================================================================

@authHost = http://localhost:4000
@blogHost = http://localhost:5000

### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. REGISTER ENDPOINTS (reader, author, admin)
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1a. Register as Reader
POST {{authHost}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "reader_sample",
  "email": "reader_sample@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "reader"
}

### 1b. Register as Author
POST {{authHost}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "author_sample",
  "email": "author_sample@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "author"
}

### 1c. Register as Admin
POST {{authHost}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin_sample",
  "email": "admin_sample@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "admin"
}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. LOGIN (Receiving accessToken & refreshToken)
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2a. Login as Author (Seeds or Registered)
# @name loginAuthor
POST {{authHost}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "author@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Variables from Author Login
@authorAccessToken = {{loginAuthor.response.body.accessToken}}
@authorRefreshToken = {{loginAuthor.response.body.refreshToken}}

### 2b. Login as Another Author (Author 2 for ownership permission test)
# @name loginAuthor2
POST {{authHost}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "author2@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Variable for Author 2
@author2AccessToken = {{loginAuthor2.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2c. Login as Reader
# @name loginReader
POST {{authHost}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "reader@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Variable for Reader
@readerAccessToken = {{loginReader.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2d. Login as Admin
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{authHost}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Variable for Admin
@adminAccessToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. REFRESH TOKEN (Exchanges refreshToken for a new accessToken)
### --------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{authHost}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{authorRefreshToken}}"
}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. LOGOUT (Revokes refreshToken in DB)
### --------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{authHost}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{authorRefreshToken}}"
}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. PUBLIC BLOG ENDPOINTS
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5a. Public GET all posts
GET {{blogHost}}/api/posts

### 5b. Public GET post by ID
GET {{blogHost}}/api/posts/1


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. CREATE POST ROLE ENFORCEMENT
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6a. Create post as Reader -> MUST RETURN 403 Forbidden
POST {{blogHost}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{readerAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Reader Trying to Post",
  "content": "This should be rejected with 403 Forbidden."
}

### 6b. Create post as Author -> MUST RETURN 201 Created
# @name createdAuthorPost
POST {{blogHost}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{authorAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Post by Author One",
  "content": "This is legitimate content published by author_one."
}

### Save Created Post ID
@createdPostId = {{createdAuthorPost.response.body.postId}}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. EDIT POST (OWNERSHIP ENFORCEMENT)
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

### 7a. Edit post as Another Author (Non-owner) -> MUST RETURN 403 Forbidden
PUT {{blogHost}}/api/posts/{{createdPostId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{author2AccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Unauthorized Modification Attempt",
  "content": "Should be rejected because author2 does not own this post."
}

### 7b. Edit post as Author (Owner) -> MUST RETURN 200 OK
PUT {{blogHost}}/api/posts/{{createdPostId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authorAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated by Owner (Author One)",
  "content": "Successfully updated by the legitimate owner."
}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. DELETE POST (ADMIN ONLY RESTRICTION)
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

### 8a. Delete post as Author -> MUST RETURN 403 Forbidden
DELETE {{blogHost}}/api/posts/{{createdPostId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authorAccessToken}}

### 8b. Delete post as Admin -> MUST RETURN 200 OK
DELETE {{blogHost}}/api/posts/{{createdPostId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. GET /api/me/posts (Returns ONLY logged-in user's posts)
### --------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{blogHost}}/api/me/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{authorAccessToken}}
